KORTEX PAST EXAMINATION PAPERS
WAEC - Government (Year 2020)

Q1. The primary objective of the principle of Separation of Powers is to:
  (A) Promote legislative supremacy
  (B) Prevent tyranny and protect liberty
  (C) Accelerate executive actions
  (D) Merge courts
  Answer: B - Separation of Powers divides authority among branches to prevent tyranny.


